  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>The waymarked Fenouillet trail starts from Bonporteau beach in Cavalaire-sur-Mer and reaches the Pointe du Dattier. The Fenouillet valley is a cool corner with Mediterranean riverside vegetation, then the trail offers views over the islands, Cap Lardier and the Maures massif. Allow 8 km in 3 h (360 m of elevation gain), or 3 km if you come back via the Fenouillet after the first viewpoint.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Neither Cavalaire town hall nor the tourist office gives a dog rule for this trail: keep your dog on a leash, as the path is steep and narrow in places. In summer, access to the Corniche des Maures massif is regulated from 21 June to 30 September according to the wildfire risk level: a prefectural order sets the accessible zones each day, so check the map before setting out (risque-prevention-incendie.fr/var, also at the tourist office). Bring water for your dog and avoid the hottest hours.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: set off early in the morning or late in the day in summer, the ground is cooler under your paws.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The trail continues beyond the Pointe du Dattier for the more motivated, or can be kept as a shorter round trip from Cavalaire.</p>
